\abstract(
Study the actual native producer from a tiny, inspectable example through the
retained original experiment and explicit boundary/work controls. Complete
editable C++ programs own every rendered native figure.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and scope

The native producer trial-factors the exact base order, solves each base-q digit
by a linear candidate scan, then merges the solved prime-power residues by CRT.
Its digit search is O(q), rather than a square-root subgroup solver or a
prebuilt lookup table. Trial factoring has its own cost and explicit
selected-call policy. Finite-field membership and the exact base order are
checked before digit solving. The original modulus1009, base11, order1008 and
secret777 are retained; no external dataset is relevant.

$$ x=\sum_{k=0}^{e-1}d_kq^k\pmod{q^e},\qquad x\equiv x_i\pmod{q_i^{e_i}}. $$

> A tiny actual producing history

The table reads actual producing records. The native diagram names actual
captured values from that same run.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pohlig_hellman_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    auto t = dm::algorithms::pohlig_hellman_trace(2, 8, 13, 12);
    std::print("\n| subgroup prime | actual digit index | reduced target | actual picked digit | candidate " "tests | actual residue after |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &r : t.digits)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", r.prime, r.index,
                   r.target, r.digit, r.candidate_tests, r.after);
    std::print("\n| actual CRT factor | residue | previous value | previous modulus | value after | combined " "modulus |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &r : t.merges)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", r.modulus, r.residue,
                   r.previous_value, r.previous_modulus, r.after,
                   r.combined_modulus);

    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual first linear digit\nq={}, digit={}",
                       t.digits[0].prime, t.digits[0].digit));
    d.node("n1", {9, 0},
           std::format("Actual first CRT state\nx={} mod{}", t.merges[0].after,
                       t.merges[0].combined_modulus));
    d.node("n2", {18, 0},
           std::format("Actual equation-verified result\nx={}, found={}",
                       t.run.exponent, t.run.found));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/pohlig_hellman_tiny.svg");
}
```
