> API and interpretation

Every block is a complete editable C++ program. Reusable searches, walks,
geometry decisions, fixture histories and algorithm work live in the canonical
library. Captured records own their values and are not reconstructed by a second
algorithm in the report. Explicit policies count the documented selected calls,
records or scalar entries; they are not peak-byte or wall-clock budgets.
Original reference curves are labelled as references, and finite returned
results are not promoted into universal convergence, recovery, scaling or speed
guarantees.

Python arbitrary-precision powers, inverse powers and CRT check actual reduced
targets, linear-search digits and merge states. Frozen primitive-base
comparisons preserve three hundred ordinary solutions. The shared batch passes83
native regression tests,18 directly instrumented sanitizer tests,84 compiled and
executed public examples,391/391 scoped documentation definitions, standalone
and installed header checks, a linked installed consumer and ten representative
symbol hovers. All four complete programs execute and their computed results and
local figures survive HTML and Markdown export. Build receipts:
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-284-293/`.
